Z||000000||Spektyr||04-26-2001||11:21 PM||||After spending the entire day working on my Fiero, getting a mild sunburn, losing a bit of blood, and cursing many times, she started up!  While the work was relatively minor, I'm still quite pleased.<P>What I did:<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Oil change with Bosch filter and 10w-40 oil<BR><LI>New Bosch distributer and rotor<BR><LI>New Accel coil and ignition module<BR><LI>New Splitfire sparkplugs and wires<BR><LI>Low temp thermostat and fan switch<BR><LI>New GT logo on the front facia<BR></UL><P>She gave me some pretty serious grief on the number 6 plug, but I think it was just to test me, see if I'd be a good owner for her.  She fired right up for me and ran smoothly (and MUCH cooler) on the short test drive to the gas station to feed her, and Wendy's to feed me.  (Duh, she comes first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>No real seat-of-the pants difference, but I didn't really open her up too much.  Tomorrow I'll be rebuilding the headlight motors and removing a restriction in the exhaust (catalytic converter).<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||10
